+# Dealer audit reconciliation (DA-01 … DA-07)
+
+Each finding from `docs/handover/DEALER-ACCOUNT-20261121/DEALER-ACCOUNT-DEFECT-AND-RISK-REGISTER.md` was re-checked against the current source (`origin/main` 1eb1489) and a freshly built disposable database before it was changed. Status labels: VERIFIED (executed, evidence), BLOCKED, NOT TESTED.
+
+| ID | Original finding | Current reproduction | Root cause | Fix | Regression test | Final status |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| DA-01 | Mark sold while a funded escrow / accepted-offer settlement is open | Reproduced on the pre-change code: plain two-field update, no lock check | `dealerListingSale.service.js` only checked "already sold" and live auction | Atomic SQL function `kayad_dealer_listing_lifecycle_atomic` (row lock, escrow / purchase-outcome / settlement / bids checks, one transaction). 409 codes `TRANSACTION_LOCK`, `OFFER_SETTLEMENT_LOCK`, `AUCTION_OR_BID_LOCK`. Triggers on `escrows` and `marketplace_offer_settlements` take a shared lock on the car row and refuse to open a new transaction on a listing the owner already sold | Journey 09 (individual, bulk, funded escrow, accepted offer, release then legitimate sale, 12 + 8 concurrent race rounds); Jest `dealerMarkSold`, `dealerLifecycleUnits` | VERIFIED |
+| DA-02 | Bulk "sold" inconsistent (status sold, sold flag false, no sale record) | Reproduced: bulk endpoints wrote `status` only | Two independent writers (`bulkUpdateListings`, `/cars/bulk-status`) | Both endpoints call `bulkChangeDealerListingStatus`, which uses the same atomic function per listing (itemised result with per-id reason codes; duplicates collapsed; max 100). `sold_at` and a sale record are written in the same transaction | Journey 09 (mixed selection, duplicates, foreign ids, all-blocked 409, concurrency); Jest `stage5aSellerSelfPublication`, `stage1ListingWriteBoundaries` | VERIFIED |
+| DA-03 | Sold listing still editable (price changed to 1) | Reproduced | Dealer roles skipped the mutation guard | `assertPersonalListingMutationAllowed` now refuses edit / photos / remove on sold listings for business roles (409 `LISTING_SOLD_READ_ONLY`); DB trigger `trg_cars_sold_read_only` is the final backstop (status, sold flag, title, price, photos, description, owner, `deleted_at`). Admin correction only through `kayad_admin_correct_sold_listing` (admin role, reason ≥ 10 chars, audited) | Journey 09 (PUT, cover, reorder, delete, bulk delete, pause / republish, 5 direct SQL updates, admin function incl. non-admin and missing reason) | VERIFIED |
+| DA-04 | Banking saved but read back blank | Reproduced: GET returned cached blank for 5 minutes; `?x=1` bypassed it | `invalidateCache("dealer")` passed a bare string to Redis `SCAN MATCH`, which matches no key (`dealer:<id>:<path>:<query>`), so no write ever invalidated any dealer cache | `normalizeInvalidationPattern` (bare prefix → `prefix:*`); `GET /settlement` is no longer cached and sends `Cache-Control: private, no-store`; PUT reads back the stored row; masked fields added; UI re-reads after save and shows a masked summary | Journey 10 (19 checks: save → read-back → re-login → update merge → invalid input → clear → tenant isolation → five staff roles denied → audit without values); node:test `dealerLifecycleUnits` | VERIFIED |
